{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need an architect to design a new house in North York?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Houses are exempt from the requirement for an architect in Ontario, so a designer qualified with a BCIN in the House category can design the house and prepare the permit drawings. You can still choose to work with an architect."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the City of Toronto check before a new house is approved?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The building permit review checks the drawings against the Ontario Building Code and the zoning by-law for the lot, including height, setbacks, lot coverage and floor area. If the design goes beyond the zoning limits, it needs a minor variance from the Committee of Adjustment first."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you design only the facade of a new house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Some clients come to us for the exterior only, with the facade, materials and lighting designed in 3D, while others want the full house, including interiors and permit drawings."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you redesign the facade of an existing house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We design new fronts for existing houses as part of a renovation or addition, with new cladding, windows, porch and lighting, and prepare the permit drawings when the work needs a permit."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Which areas do you work in?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"North York and the rest of Toronto, Vaughan, Richmond Hill, Etobicoke and the wider Greater Toronto Area."}}]}
